A||N||6||Jhonny||Strange oxygen sensor problem.||||4||
Z||000000||Jhonny||08-06-2001||02:30 AM||||Hi,<P>My Fieros tailpipes was starting to get sooty and the fuel consumption went up 25-30% or so.<BR>But otherwise no problems no check engine light was coming on or any other problems as poor performance.<BR>I decided that I will check all sensors to start with and first of all the oxygen sensor.<BR>When I tried to find the sensor cable running from the sensor I just found a hole where the sensor was supposed to be in the y pipe. The center part of the sensor was dangling freely at the end of the cable still doing some kind of work because no code was set. It had broke apart into two pieces.<BR>Has someone out there experienced this before ? <BR>The sensor looked to me as it was of 'el cheapo' brand.<P>/// Jhonny<P>------------------<BR>Jhonny Sokura<BR>Vadstena, Östergötland Sweden<P><A HREF="http://home.swipnet.se/jks/fiero3.jpg" TARGET=_blank> Pontiac Fiero GT -87 , V6 5spd<BR> </A>||||reg||4
Z||000001||PBJ||08-06-2001||10:58 AM||||Yes actually it is more common than what you would think, and strange that no code would be set, but in the mid 80's it takes alot to go wrong with o2 sensor for the ecm to pick it up-especially the 4 cyl,<P>now in todays cars if the "blink" the ses light comes on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-06-2001||01:39 PM||||whats an oxygen sensor?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000003||theogre||08-06-2001||08:00 PM||||I've seen them do that. Hitting them with water when they are hot can do it. sometimes it's just aging of the metal.<P>buy a good Bosch sensor to replace it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jhonny||08-07-2001||01:54 AM||||Thanks,<P>Is it a unheated 18 mm zirconia sensor ?<BR>How about converting to a heated type of sensor any known advantages ?<P>/// Jhonny||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||08-07-2001||07:31 PM||||There is no reason to change sensor type on most cars. You would only need a heated one in a header that could't keep it hot enough.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jhonny||08-08-2001||02:00 AM||||<BR>Propably the failure of the O2 sensor also fried my catalytic converter.<BR>I think the O2 sensor hasn't been operational<BR>for a long time.<P>Thanks<P>/// Jhonny||||reg||1
